[14:26:22] Hook fired. Input: {"session_id":"ea26eeef-6b8c-47d6-8920-c2a9ed971158","transcript_path":"/Users/sid-j/.claude/projects/-Users-sid-j-ai-chief-of-staff/ea26eeef-6b8c-47d6-8920-c2a9ed971158.jsonl","cwd":"/Users/sid-j/ai-chief-of-staff","permission_mode":"default","hook_event_name":"PostToolUse","tool_name":"WebSearch","tool_input":{"query":"Google Calendar MCP calendarmcp.googleapis.com authentication oauth setup"},"tool_response":{"query":"Google Calendar MCP calendarmcp.googleapis.com authentication oauth setup","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_8df2e1be8e7d7d3f6f7d613a","content":[{"title":"API Documentation — Calendar MCP — CalendarMCP","url":"https://calendarmcp.ai/docs"},{"title":"docs/authentication.md at main · nspady/google-calendar-mcp","url":"https://github.com/nspady/google-calendar-mcp/blob/main/docs/authentication.md"},{"title":"nspady/google-calendar-mcp","url":"https://github.com/nspady/google-calendar-mcp"},{"title":"Homoney/Google-Calendar-MCP-Server","url":"https://github.com/dhomoney/Google-Calendar-MCP-Server"},{"title":"docs/authentication.md at HEAD · nspady/google-calendar-mcp","url":"https://github.com/nspady/google-calendar-mcp/blob/HEAD/docs/authentication.md"}]},"## Web Search Results: Google Calendar MCP Authentication & OAuth Setup\n\nI found comprehensive results covering Google Calendar MCP authentication and OAuth setup. Here's what I discovered:\n\n---\n\n### 1. **CalendarMCP (calendarmcp.ai)** - Hosted Service\nA hosted MCP service for Google Calendar with:\n- **OAuth** or service-account sharing options\n- Multi-account support with per-calendar permissions\n- Read/Write matrix for access control\n- Endpoint: `https://calendarmcp.ai/api/mcp`\n\n---\n\n### 2. **nspady/google-calendar-mcp** (Most Popular - 1,093 Stars)\nThe leading open-source TypeScript implementation. Key setup steps:\n\n**Google Cloud Setup:**\n1. Create project in [Google Cloud Console](https://console.cloud.google.com)\n2. Enable Google Calendar API\n3. Create OAuth 2.0 credentials:\n   - Choose **Desktop app** type (critical!)\n   - Add scopes: `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.events` or broader `calendar` scope\n   - Add your email as a **test user** and wait 2-3 minutes for propagation\n4. Download credentials → save as `gcp-oauth.keys.json`\n\n**Credential File Format:**\n```json\n{\n  \"installed\": {\n    \"project_id\": \"YOUR_PROJECT_ID\",\n    \"client_id\": \"YOUR_CLIENT_ID.apps.googleusercontent.com\",\n    \"client_secret\": \"YOUR_CLIENT_SECRET\",\n    \"auth_uri\": \"https://accounts.google.com/o/oauth2/auth\",\n    \"token_uri\": \"https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token\",\n    \"redirect_uris\": [\"http://localhost\"]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Configuration Options:**\n- **Environment Variable (Recommended):** `GOOGLE_OAUTH_CREDENTIALS=\"/path/to/gcp-oauth.keys.json\"`\n- **Default Location:** Project root as `gcp-oauth.keys.json`\n\n**Token Storage:**\n- macOS/Linux: `~/.config/google-calendar-mcp/tokens.json`\n- Windows: `%APPDATA%\\google-calendar-mcp\\tokens.json`\n\n**First-Time Authentication:**\n1. Start Claude Desktop after configuration\n2. Server automatically opens browser for OAuth\n3. Grant calendar permissions\n4. Return to Claude - ready to use!\n\n**Important Notes:**\n- While in **test mode**, tokens expire after **7 days**\n- To avoid weekly re-auth: publish app to production mode in Google Cloud Console\n- **Security:** Never commit credentials to git, use `chmod 600` on credential files\n\n---\n\n### 3. **dhomoney/Google-Calendar-MCP-Server** (Python Alternative)\nA Python-based MCP server with similar functionality:\n- Credentials: `~/.config/google-calendar-mcp/credentials.json`\n- Token: `~/.config/google-calendar-mcp/token.json`\n- Supports list_events, get_event, search_events, create_event, list_calendars\n\n---\n\n### Key Takeaways\n\n| Aspect | Details |\n|--------|---------|\n| **OAuth Type** | Desktop app (not web application) |\n| **Required Scopes** | `calendar.events` or full `calendar` |\n| **Test Mode** | Tokens expire after 7 days |\n| **Test Users** | Must add email in OAuth consent screen |\n| **Multi-Account** | Supported with `manage-accounts` tool |\n| **Security** | Never commit credentials, secure file permissions |\n\nWould you like more details on any specific aspect of the setup process?"],"durationSeconds":27.111857334},"tool_use_id":"call_function_mruvdoqa7y0t_1"}
