[14:26:53] Hook fired. Input: {"session_id":"ea26eeef-6b8c-47d6-8920-c2a9ed971158","transcript_path":"/Users/sid-j/.claude/projects/-Users-sid-j-ai-chief-of-staff/ea26eeef-6b8c-47d6-8920-c2a9ed971158.jsonl","cwd":"/Users/sid-j/ai-chief-of-staff","permission_mode":"default","hook_event_name":"PostToolUse","tool_name":"WebFetch","tool_input":{"url":"https://github.com/nspady/google-calendar-mcp/blob/main/docs/authentication.md","prompt":"Extract the full authentication setup instructions, OAuth consent screen requirements, and any troubleshooting steps"},"tool_response":{"bytes":317489,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"\n\n## Google Calendar MCP Authentication Setup\n\n### Google Cloud Configuration\n\n1. **Create a project** in Google Cloud Console and enable the Google Calendar API\n2. **Create OAuth 2.0 credentials** via \"APIs & Services\" → \"Credentials\"\n3. **Application type must be \"Desktop app\"** (critical requirement)\n4. **Download credentials** as `gcp-oauth.keys.json`\n\n### OAuth Consent Screen Requirements\n\n- Select \"External\" user type\n- Provide: App name, User support email, Developer contact information\n- Add scopes: `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.events` or broader `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar`\n- Add test users (your email address)\n- **Wait 2-3 minutes** for test users to propagate before attempting authentication\n\nThe documentation notes: \"Including `project_id` is important to avoid 'User Rate Limit Exceeded' errors.\"\n\n### Credential Storage Options\n\n**Option 1 (Recommended):** Set `GOOGLE_OAUTH_CREDENTIALS` environment variable\n\n**Option 2:** Place file as `gcp-oauth.keys.json` in project root\n\nTokens are stored at `~/.config/google-calendar-mcp/tokens.json` (macOS/Linux) or `%APPDATA%\\google-calendar-mcp\\tokens.json` (Windows).\n\n### Troubleshooting\n\n| Error | Solution |\n|-------|----------|\n| \"Invalid credentials\" | Ensure \"Desktop app\" selected; verify valid JSON and correct file path |\n| \"Access blocked\" | Add email as test user; wait 2-3 minutes for propagation |\n| \"Token expired\" | Re-authenticate via `npm run auth`; check if in test mode |\n\n### Test Mode Limitations\n\nTest mode tokens expire after 7 days. For personal use, simply re-authenticate weekly as needed.","durationMs":20521,"url":"https://github.com/nspady/google-calendar-mcp/blob/main/docs/authentication.md"},"tool_use_id":"call_function_g1icxd2roc62_1"}
