[14:28:57] Hook fired. Input: {"session_id":"ea26eeef-6b8c-47d6-8920-c2a9ed971158","transcript_path":"/Users/sid-j/.claude/projects/-Users-sid-j-ai-chief-of-staff/ea26eeef-6b8c-47d6-8920-c2a9ed971158.jsonl","cwd":"/Users/sid-j/ai-chief-of-staff","permission_mode":"default","hook_event_name":"PostToolUse","tool_name":"WebSearch","tool_input":{"query":"\"does not support dynamic client registration\" Google Calendar MCP oauth error fix"},"tool_response":{"query":"\"does not support dynamic client registration\" Google Calendar MCP oauth error fix","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_11e69db4a640c4325c022df5","content":[{"title":"MCP OAuth: \"does not support dynamic client registration\" despite clientId configured · Issue #38102 · anthropics/claude-code","url":"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/38102"},{"title":"Bug: Dynamic Client Registration Requires Both authorization_code and refresh_token Grant Types · Issue #2460 · PrefectHQ/fastmcp","url":"https://github.com/PrefectHQ/fastmcp/issues/2460"},{"title":"Updated from 1.16.2 to 1.17.3 and seeing OAuth error: invalid_scope - Client was not registered with scope https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar · Issue #675 · taylorwilsdon/google_workspace_mcp","url":"https://github.com/taylorwilsdon/google_workspace_mcp/issues/675"},{"title":"Support pre-configured OAuth client credentials without requiring Dynamic Client Registration · Issue #26675 · anthropics/claude-code","url":"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/26675"},{"title":"Dynamic Client Registration(DCR) issues in MCP Servers · Issue #279955 · microsoft/vscode","url":"https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/issues/279955"}]},"## Search Results Summary\n\nThe search returned several relevant GitHub issues discussing the \"does not support dynamic client registration\" error in the context of MCP OAuth. Here's what I found:\n\n### Key Issues\n\n1. **Issue #38102** (Anthropic/claude-code) - Primary bug report with detailed reproduction steps\n   - Status: Open, labeled as bug/duplicate\n   - Affects: AWS Cognito and similar OAuth providers that don't support DCR\n   - Even when `clientId` is explicitly configured in `.mcp.json`, Claude Code ignores it and attempts dynamic client registration\n\n2. **Issue #26675** (Anthropic/claude-code) - Core feature request\n   - Status: Open (17 👍 reactions)\n   - Title: \"Support pre-configured OAuth client credentials without requiring Dynamic Client Registration\"\n   - Affects: Azure AD/Entra ID, enterprise environments with pre-registered OAuth apps, GitHub's official MCP server\n\n3. **Issue #675** (google_workspace_mcp) - Google Calendar MCP\n   - Status: Closed (different error)\n   - The `invalid_scope` error was a misconfiguration issue on the user's side\n\n### The Problem\n\nEven with this configuration:\n```json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"my-server\": {\n      \"type\": \"http\",\n      \"url\": \"https://my-server.example.com/mcp/\",\n      \"oauth\": {\n        \"clientId\": \"my-pre-registered-client-id\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nClaude Code still:\n1. Fetches authorization server metadata\n2. Looks for `registration_endpoint`\n3. Fails with \"Incompatible auth server: does not support dynamic client registration\"\n\n### Workarounds\n\n1. **Bearer Token via Environment Variable** (currently working):\n   ```json\n   {\n     \"mcpServers\": {\n       \"my-server\": {\n         \"type\": \"http\",\n         \"url\": \"https://my-server.example.com/mcp/\",\n         \"headers\": {\n           \"Authorization\": \"Bearer ${MY_TOKEN}\"\n         }\n       }\n     }\n   }\n   ```\n   Use a helper script for OAuth PKCE flow, then launch `claude` from that shell.\n\n2. **mcp-stdio bridge** (from issue #38102):\n   ```json\n   {\n     \"mcpServers\": {\n       \"my-server\": {\n         \"command\": \"mcp-stdio\",\n         \"args\": [\n           \"--oauth\",\n           \"--client-id\", \"my-cognito-client-id\",\n           \"--oauth-scope\", \"openid profile\",\n           \"https://my-server.example.com/mcp/\"\n         ]\n       }\n     }\n   }\n   ```\n\n### Additional Bug (Zod Validation)\n\nIf `registration_endpoint` is returned as `null` in the metadata, there's a Zod validation error: `\"expected string, received null\"`.\n\n---\n\n### Related: VS Code\n\nVS Code had similar DCR issues (Issue #279955) but these appear to have been **fixed** in VS Code Insiders as of December 2025/January 2026. The root cause was related to Protected Resource Metadata (PRM) validation not matching the spec requirements for `resource` values."],"durationSeconds":29.48739954099999},"tool_use_id":"call_function_8wh4sdghnqlt_1"}
