[14:29:22] Hook fired. Input: {"session_id":"ea26eeef-6b8c-47d6-8920-c2a9ed971158","transcript_path":"/Users/sid-j/.claude/projects/-Users-sid-j-ai-chief-of-staff/ea26eeef-6b8c-47d6-8920-c2a9ed971158.jsonl","cwd":"/Users/sid-j/ai-chief-of-staff","permission_mode":"default","hook_event_name":"PostToolUse","tool_name":"WebFetch","tool_input":{"url":"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/38102","prompt":"Extract the workaround solutions and any configuration fixes for this specific error"},"tool_response":{"bytes":293862,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"\n\n## Workaround Solutions for MCP OAuth Dynamic Client Registration Error\n\nBased on this GitHub issue (#38102), there are **no complete workarounds** currently—this is a confirmed bug. However, the issue provides partial insights and configuration details that may help:\n\n### Configuration That Triggers the Error\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"my-server\": {\n      \"type\": \"http\",\n      \"url\": \"https://my-server.example.com/mcp/\",\n      \"oauth\": {\n        \"clientId\": \"my-cognito-client-id\",\n        \"callbackPort\": 19876\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Partial Observations\n\n1. **Setting `registration_endpoint` to `null`** causes a Zod validation error:\n   ```\n   \"expected string, received null\" on registration_endpoint path\n   ```\n\n2. **Removing `registration_endpoint` entirely** from the OAuth metadata avoids the validation error but still triggers the dynamic registration attempt.\n\n### Recommended Fix Needed (from issue)\n\nClaude Code should:\n- Use the pre-configured `clientId` directly for the OAuth authorization code flow when provided\n- Skip dynamic client registration (RFC 7591) when `clientId` is already configured\n- Handle `null` values for `registration_endpoint` properly in Zod validation\n\n### Environment Context\n\n- **OAuth Provider**: AWS Cognito (custom domain) - does **not** support dynamic client registration\n- **PKCE (S256)**: Supported by both server and Cognito\n- **Platform**: macOS Darwin 25.3.0\n\n### Related Command Attempted\n\n```bash\nclaude mcp add --transport http --client-id <id> --callback-port 19876 my-server https://...\n```\n\n**Status**: The issue is marked as `[duplicate]` - indicating this bug may already be tracked elsewhere or under active development.","durationMs":18989,"url":"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/38102"},"tool_use_id":"call_function_pmiugrdxlwah_1"}
