[14:29:43] Hook fired. Input: {"session_id":"ea26eeef-6b8c-47d6-8920-c2a9ed971158","transcript_path":"/Users/sid-j/.claude/projects/-Users-sid-j-ai-chief-of-staff/ea26eeef-6b8c-47d6-8920-c2a9ed971158.jsonl","cwd":"/Users/sid-j/ai-chief-of-staff","permission_mode":"default","hook_event_name":"PostToolUse","tool_name":"WebFetch","tool_input":{"url":"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/26675","prompt":"Extract the full issue details, status, and any workaround options"},"tool_response":{"bytes":298907,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Issue #26675: Support Pre-configured OAuth Client Credentials Without Dynamic Client Registration\n\n**Repository:** anthropics/claude-code  \n**Status:** Open  \n**Opened by:** danwritecode (Feb 18, 2026)\n\n## Problem\n\nClaude Code's OAuth implementation requires Dynamic Client Registration (DCR) even when a `clientId` is pre-configured in `.mcp.json`, making Azure AD/Entra ID and other enterprise OAuth providers incompatible.\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nEven with this configuration, the pre-configured `clientId` is ignored:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"my-server\": {\n      \"type\": \"http\",\n      \"url\": \"http://localhost:5042/mcp\",\n      \"oauth\": {\n        \"clientId\": \"xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nClaude Code still fetches authorization server metadata, looks for `registration_endpoint`, and fails with: **\"Incompatible auth server: does not support dynamic client registration\"**\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nWhen `oauth.clientId` is provided, Claude Code should:\n1. Skip the DCR check entirely\n2. Use the pre-configured client ID for the OAuth flow\n3. Proceed directly to authorization\n\n## Workarounds Attempted\n\nUsers had to implement:\n1. A fake `/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server` endpoint proxying Azure AD metadata\n2. A `/register` DCR endpoint returning pre-configured credentials\n3. Workarounds still fail due to `resource` parameter/scope mismatches (AADSTS9010)\n\n## Proposed Solution\n\nWhen `oauth.clientId` is present:\n1. Skip checking for `registration_endpoint` in authorization server metadata\n2. Skip the DCR call to `/register`\n3. Use the configured `clientId` directly\n\nThis aligns with the MCP spec where DCR is a \"SHOULD\", not a \"MUST\".\n\n## Impact\n\n- All Azure AD/Entra ID users\n- Enterprise environments with pre-registered OAuth apps\n- GitHub's official MCP server (github/github-mcp-server#549)\n- Any OAuth provider that doesn't support DCR","durationMs":17480,"url":"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/26675"},"tool_use_id":"call_function_wvrds9ye24e8_1"}
