[14:29:50] Hook fired. Input: {"session_id":"ea26eeef-6b8c-47d6-8920-c2a9ed971158","transcript_path":"/Users/sid-j/.claude/projects/-Users-sid-j-ai-chief-of-staff/ea26eeef-6b8c-47d6-8920-c2a9ed971158.jsonl","cwd":"/Users/sid-j/ai-chief-of-staff","permission_mode":"default","hook_event_name":"Stop","stop_hook_active":false,"last_assistant_message":"You're right — this is a known issue. The `calendarmcp.googleapis.com/mcp/v1` server **doesn't support Dynamic Client Registration (DCR)**, which Claude Code requires. That's why you're seeing the error.\n\n**Your options:**\n\n1. **Use an alternative MCP server that supports DCR** (recommended by the GitHub issue):\n   - **[nspady/google-calendar-mcp](https://github.com/nspady/google-calendar-mcp)** — self-hosted TypeScript server, supports proper OAuth\n   - **Composio** — provides a managed Google Calendar MCP with working OAuth\n\n2. **Use stdio transport** instead of HTTP with an alternative server\n\n**To fix with nspady's server:**\n\n```bash\n# Install\nnpm install -g google-calendar-mcp\n\n# Add to settings.json via stdio transport\nclaude mcp add gcal --command google-calendar-mcp\n```\n\nOr configure the environment variable for credentials:\n```json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"gcal\": {\n      \"command\": \"google-calendar-mcp\",\n      \"env\": {\n        \"GOOGLE_OAUTH_CREDENTIALS\": \"/path/to/gcp-oauth.keys.json\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nWould you like me to help you set up nspady's google-calendar-mcp server as an alternative?"}
