[14:46:41] Hook fired. Input: {"session_id":"ea26eeef-6b8c-47d6-8920-c2a9ed971158","transcript_path":"/Users/sid-j/.claude/projects/-Users-sid-j-ai-chief-of-staff/ea26eeef-6b8c-47d6-8920-c2a9ed971158.jsonl","cwd":"/Users/sid-j/ai-chief-of-staff","permission_mode":"default","hook_event_name":"PostToolUse","tool_name":"Read","tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/sid-j/ai-chief-of-staff/.claude/context/communication-style.md"},"tool_response":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sid-j/ai-chief-of-staff/.claude/context/communication-style.md","content":"# My Communication Style\n\nClaude should use this file when drafting any email, message, or reply on my behalf.\nRead this before writing anything. Match my voice, not a generic professional voice.\n\n---\n\n## The Baseline\n\n- Short. I cut aggressively. If it can be said in 2 lines, use 2 lines.\n- Direct. State the point first, context second.\n- Confident but not arrogant. I don't hedge with \"I think\" or \"just wanted to\".\n- I use contractions. I don't write like a press release.\n\n---\n\n## By Relationship Type\n\n### With my direct reports (Kai, Riya, Tom)\n- Casual, warm, first-name always\n- Short messages. Often bullet points.\n- I ask questions more than give directives. e.g. \"What's blocking you on this?\"\n- I celebrate wins specifically. Not \"great job!\" — \"That QA turnaround was fast, nice work.\"\n- I don't pepper them with follow-ups. One ask per message.\n\n### With my manager (Sarah Chen, VP Product)\n- Structured. Lead with status, then ask/issue, then recommendation.\n- Proactive over reactive — I flag things before she asks.\n- I'm direct with her; she prefers no fluff.\n- Subject lines: clear and scannable. e.g. \"Orion v2 — QA update + one decision needed\"\n\n### With executives (C-suite, board)\n- Concise and confident. No more than 3 paragraphs.\n- Lead with the business implication, not the detail.\n- Include a clear ask or FYI label so they know what action (if any) is needed.\n- No jargon. Spell out acronyms on first use.\n\n### With external partners / clients\n- Warmer opener, but still brief.\n- Professional but personable. I remember details about their context.\n- Follow-up promptly. They're not inside our org; they shouldn't have to chase.\n- Hartwell Group: extra attentive, always CC my manager.\n\n---\n\n## Things I Never Write\n\n- \"I hope this email finds you well.\"\n- \"Per my last email...\"\n- \"Just circling back\" or \"Just checking in\"\n- \"As per our conversation\"\n- \"Please don't hesitate to reach out\"\n- \"Happy to hop on a call\" (use: \"Free Tuesday 3–4pm if useful\")\n- Passive voice on decisions: not \"it was decided\" — \"we decided\"\n- Three-sentence opening before getting to the point\n\n---\n\n## Sign-offs\n\n- Team / colleagues: just my name — \"— Alex\"\n- External / formal: \"Best, Alex Johnson\"\n- Quick replies: nothing, or just \"Thanks — Alex\"\n\n---\n\n## Formatting preferences\n\n- Bullet points for lists of 3+\n- Bold for the key ask or decision in longer emails\n- Never: full caps for emphasis, multiple exclamation marks\n- Subject lines: [ACTION NEEDED] or [FYI] prefix when appropriate\n","numLines":73,"startLine":1,"totalLines":73}},"tool_use_id":"call_function_hogggqjauk47_3"}
[14:46:41] Hook fired. Input: {"session_id":"ea26eeef-6b8c-47d6-8920-c2a9ed971158","transcript_path":"/Users/sid-j/.claude/projects/-Users-sid-j-ai-chief-of-staff/ea26eeef-6b8c-47d6-8920-c2a9ed971158.jsonl","cwd":"/Users/sid-j/ai-chief-of-staff","permission_mode":"default","hook_event_name":"PostToolUse","tool_name":"Read","tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/sid-j/ai-chief-of-staff/.claude/context/my-priorities.md"},"tool_response":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sid-j/ai-chief-of-staff/.claude/context/my-priorities.md","content":"# My Priorities — Q1/Q2 2026\n\nThis file tells Claude what I'm focused on right now.\nWhen triaging email or calendar, weight actions against these priorities.\n\n---\n\n## Top 3 This Quarter\n\n1. **Ship Orion v2** — Our core product launch. Anything blocking this is P0.\n   - Hard deadline: April 15\n   - DRI: me + engineering lead (Priya)\n   - Status: in QA, one major bug open\n\n2. **Reduce churn to <8%** — Currently at 11.2%. Running win/loss interviews and\n   mid-market re-engagement campaign. Any customer escalation goes to top of queue.\n\n3. **AI Roadmap for Board** — Presenting May 3. Need 3 use cases, ROI estimates,\n   and a 12-month phasing plan. Still gathering input from sales + data team.\n\n---\n\n## Secondary Focus\n\n- Hiring: two open roles (Senior PM, Data Analyst). Interviews ongoing.\n- Pilot with Hartwell Group — strategic account, handle with care.\n- Team offsites: planning Q3 in June, nothing confirmed yet.\n\n---\n\n## What I'm Deliberately NOT doing this quarter\n\n- Taking on new product areas until Orion v2 ships\n- Attending conferences or external events\n- Committing to any new partnerships until board presentation is done\n\n---\n\n## How to use this in triage\n\n- Email/slack about Orion v2 bugs or blockers → always surface, even if from junior team\n- Anything from Hartwell Group → flag as high priority regardless of topic\n- Churn data, customer complaints → surface immediately\n- Board prep materials, AI research → medium priority, batch for afternoon review\n- Conference invites, vendor pitches, newsletters → deprioritize or archive\n","numLines":46,"startLine":1,"totalLines":46}},"tool_use_id":"call_function_hogggqjauk47_1"}
[14:46:41] Hook fired. Input: {"session_id":"ea26eeef-6b8c-47d6-8920-c2a9ed971158","transcript_path":"/Users/sid-j/.claude/projects/-Users-sid-j-ai-chief-of-staff/ea26eeef-6b8c-47d6-8920-c2a9ed971158.jsonl","cwd":"/Users/sid-j/ai-chief-of-staff","permission_mode":"default","hook_event_name":"PostToolUse","tool_name":"Read","tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/sid-j/ai-chief-of-staff/.claude/context/my-team.md"},"tool_response":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sid-j/ai-chief-of-staff/.claude/context/my-team.md","content":"# My Team & Key Stakeholders\n\nUse this file to interpret who sent an email/message, why it might matter,\nand how to handle it. Context beats guessing.\n\n---\n\n## I Report To\n\n**Sarah Chen** — VP Product\n- Direct, data-driven, high standards\n- Prefers written updates over meetings\n- If she asks a question, she usually already knows the answer — be thorough\n- Hot buttons: shipping on time, customer trust, team retention\n- Response SLA I hold myself to: same business day\n\n---\n\n## My Direct Reports\n\n**Kai Oduya** — Senior PM (Orion core)\n- Most experienced on my team. Owns Orion v2 end-to-end.\n- If Kai flags a blocker, it's real. Escalate fast.\n- Working through some scope creep issues with engineering — handle with nuance\n\n**Riya Desai** — PM (Growth & Retention)\n- Running the churn reduction workstream\n- Newer to the role, sends more check-in messages than needed — kind but firm\n- Currently mentoring her on stakeholder communication\n\n**Tom Reyes** — Associate PM\n- Onboarded 3 months ago. Smart, eager, still calibrating judgment\n- His questions often have obvious answers — coach, don't dismiss\n- Assigned to the board AI roadmap research\n\n---\n\n## Key Cross-Functional Stakeholders\n\n**Priya Nair** — Engineering Lead\n- DRI for Orion v2 engineering. Strong relationship, high trust.\n- Communicates in Slack mostly; email from her means something escalated\n- One open disagreement about v2 scope — stay collaborative, not combative\n\n**Marcus Webb** — Head of Sales\n- Strategic accounts including Hartwell Group\n- Tends to over-promise to clients; align early on what product can deliver\n- If he's CC'd on a client email to me, it needs a response today\n\n**Dana Kim** — Data Analyst (shared resource, not my report)\n- Supporting the board AI roadmap with usage data\n- Reliable but stretched thin — be specific with asks, don't pile on\n\n**Lisa Tran** — Customer Success Lead\n- First to flag churn signals. If she's emailing, there's a customer issue.\n- Build: include her in any churn-related decisions\n\n---\n\n## External Contacts\n\n**Hartwell Group** (contact: James Okafor, Director of Operations)\n- Strategic pilot account. Decision on full contract in July.\n- Always respond within 24h. Always CC Marcus and Sarah on replies.\n- They're evaluating 2 competitors. Don't give them a reason to churn.\n\n**Board Members** (for AI roadmap presentation)\n- Linda Park (chair), Robert Asante, Miriam Goldstein\n- Context-light — assume they don't know internal acronyms\n- Treat any inbound from them as high priority\n\n---\n\n## Noise to Filter\n\n- Automated reports (analytics, uptime, billing) → archive unless anomaly\n- Newsletter subscriptions → archive\n- Vendor / recruiter cold outreach → archive\n- All-hands calendar invites from HR → accept silently, no reply needed\n","numLines":80,"startLine":1,"totalLines":80}},"tool_use_id":"call_function_hogggqjauk47_2"}
